## DialKey overlay — Help budget

**Overlay Rev.1** — 2026-09-13

DialKey layers: `docs/spec.md` (public, English) / `.cursor/rules/private_spec.md`
(Japanese OK) / tray About / `docs/*.md` → GitHub Pages.

### In Help

- What DialKey is (one line)
- How to open (default **X2**) / instant digit vs `+` then Enter / first-line `+` cue / Search / cancel
- Where to register tools (Settings → Slots)
- Switch books: mode button (X1) then 0–9, or tray → Mode
- Docs-site link (`docsUrl`), version, optional language-pack line
- Load overwrite warning only (copies into `settings/`; does not keep using the backup)
- One line: some numpads wake slowly — watch the typing window that keys registered

### Not in Help

- Architecture, performance rationale, Plan / future-vision
- Exclusive fullscreen, laptop without numpad `+`, which wireless pad to buy
- Backup / Load **steps**, Settings → Mode / Keys / Triggers (Advanced)
- Maintainer release steps, VirusTotal, packaging

The public docs site is install / FAQ / slots / configuration / privacy only.
Help string IDs: `HELP_*` / `help_about_*` in `lang/*.toml`.
